{"kind":"propose","text":"P1 source plan before code, at reviewed main 694a8c7f83deedb4e8d34706c51203029726121a. Promise 3acac812 covers request bea87570. CF-1 is on main and cutover END 53d5a148 completed, so the side lane is eligible. This act prepares no source and claims no run.\n\n1. Definition and metadata. Add an independent typed definition in examples/lending/publisher-definition.ts, with separate canonical JSON/pin if its consumer needs pinned bytes. Proposed definition name: lending-publisher. Reuse only read-only thing/content/unique declarations where useful; do not refactor or change definition.ts, definition.json, pin.ts, the old shelf browser, or hosted configuration. The new library keeps founder and gains optional publisher party, optional repository record {host,namespace,name}, optional commit head, and optional fact cursor. It has no destination field or reference. The six circulation acts keep their existing guards/state effects but send nothing.\n\nAdd bind-repository (staff, repository unset), appoint-publisher (staff, replace party), published (publish permission, appointed signer, checked fact, same-scope comparison, base equals head including both absent), and adopt-head (staff). published stores commit/head and through/cursor. Its through field names the five mapped act kinds under the new definition; both isFact(through) and equals(part(through,scope),theScope) remain explicit. New definition has no receives, timed effects, capabilities or sends. Preserve the explicit note's optional repository; an unbound publisher stops without writing.\n\nThe required lending.publish agent grant has a pending release boundary: request 38c7c579 asks whether P1 uses a separate manifest/role table under examples/lending/publisher/ or changes the named existing role/manifest only after CUT-R R2 under a new reviewed metadata baseline. Until ruled, change neither current role table nor manifest.\n\n2. Publication map and deterministic fold. Add publisher-map.ts with exactly donate-\u003efields.page/fields.content, borrow/return/cancel-\u003eopening donate.page/current fields.content, and publish-\u003enamed thing's opening donate.page/current fields.content. Add publisher-fold.ts. Its inputs are the earlier checked tree, immutable complete journal slice/opening entries and map. Process journal order; the last mapped write to a path wins. Fetch opening entries through the client before folding; the fold itself reads no live item state, filesystem, clock, credential or service. Invalid or conflicting paths skip that entry and produce a deterministic entry/reason line in the message.\n\nReuse dap-git's Reader, idOf, snapshotFiles and tree builder. snapshotCommit itself is parentless with fixed time, so it is not the publication commit: build the example's commit header with one exact base parent (none initially), one fixed author/committer text and UTC time derived from the through entry. Trailer encodes full scope ID plus genesis, through seq plus hash, and earlier head. The reader and publisher share this pure fold and byte construction. Resource/read failure stops the cycle, never substitutes an empty tree or partial journal.\n\n3. Scope and custody boundaries. Add publisher.ts plus one publisher script under examples/lending/scripts. Every scope exchange goes through stable client APIs: summary for the live library; signerSessionRequest/requestSession/Session.reader for a whole journal; ScopeHandle.log with coverage whole on every page and all continuations; entry for opening facts; declaredHandle for shaped published intents; Custody and client/node fileStore for durable keep/read-back-before-submit. Check full scope incarnation/definition, summary completeness, cursor hash, required journal coverage and fixed read head before acting. Refused, archived, filtered or incomplete reads stop without signing/pushing.\n\nA terminal answer ends one custody operation. Lost TransportError becomes custody Lost, and recovery resubmits/settles the same stored signed envelope, grants and beside data; it never invokes the build callback to replace an unresolved intent. A base refusal restarts from library. Declared transitions also require expected revisions; revision-moved can precede the base guard, so reconcile from library on that definitive refusal too. The stale-base witness supplies the fresh revision to isolate the base guard.\n\n4. Git boundary and loop. Add publisher-git.ts using existing GitProgram/nodeExec, Git.readRef/fetch/send and Reader. A cycle checks appointed member and configured repository, selects mapped work after cursor, reads branch, builds and attempts one exact compare-and-set when it equals recorded head. On refusal/lost Git reply, read the branch. A sole child of recorded head is reportable only when its trailer and reconstructed exact commit match. All other branch states stop without signing; staff may adopt-head. Then keep and submit the report. After a definitive competing report, restart from current library. No operation/outcome/preparation/delivery is introduced.\n\nGit credential request c7a68450 remains open: existing hardened local bare-Git APIs suffice for all witnesses, but no owner-credential authenticated connector for this member route exists in the API read. Do not impersonate the platform Gateway's sealed-mint token lifecycle. Proposed first script uses local bare Git, pending planner confirmation. The owner retains the credential/revocation duty; no deployment credential, provider call or secret read belongs to these witnesses.\n\n5. Test support, reader and paths. Extend examples/lending/test-support.ts with a separate maker for the new definition, leaving make/old consumers intact. A local test Transport accepts the caller's signed envelope, evaluates real restricted rules and native in-memory judges, returns original receipts for accepted-before, and exposes the needed client summary/log/entry/settle interface. It is test support, not a production scope adapter. Explicit grants model agent permissions; Session/membership authority stays labelled scripted. Retain actual rule-input bytes and definition/foreign bytes in MemorySource for verify(...,{mode:replay,grants:as-recorded}); a state refold alone is not a consistent replay report.\n\nAdd scripts/check-shelf.ts as a reader of a local clone and complete journal export. It reconstructs each publisher trailer's commit and compares all bytes, not merely branch/trailer fields. Treat a staff-adopted external head as a stated baseline, not a fold-produced commit. Keep all source, tests, scripts, config and docs in examples/lending. Update that example's Vitest/TypeScript includes for the new owner without touching root configs or any forbidden package.\n\nNine-witness map, all in proposed examples/lending/publisher.test.ts:\n1. \"donate and borrow publish one folded shelf page and exact through trailer\": real judges + client + bare Git; clone shelf/pot.md equals borrow content, one report, deterministic commit.\n2. \"restart after the ref update reports the same commit without another branch commit\": terminate publisher instance after CAS, reopen real temporary file custody, new instance reconstructs branch child and reports it.\n3. \"two publisher processes allow one ref update and one accepted report\": two independent instances of the appointed member, with distinct scripted signing identities/custody, gate both at the same captured base; count CAS success, accepted report and other definitive scope refusal. No sleeps.\n4. \"an external branch writer stops signing until staff adopts its head\": move local bare branch, assert zero report signatures, adopt-head via judge/client path, add next mapped act and publish from adopted base.\n5. \"another agent with publish permission cannot report for the appointed member\": explicitly grant both agent identities lending.publish, appoint one, show the other's signer guard refusal.\n6. \"a published report with an earlier base is refused without moving head or cursor\": use fresh expected revision so base guard decides, preserve both slots.\n7. \"the publisher journal replays consistently without outside-operation input forms\": verify MemorySource reports consistent with authority trust explicit; every entry input excludes outcome/preparation/delivery, every act send list stays empty.\n8. \"the reader reproduces publisher commits and rejects one changed file\": run shared reader/script over clone + exported journal; rewrite one content blob/tree under the same parent/trailer and require mismatch.\n9. \"a same-definition foreign through fact cannot move this cursor\": supply the real other ledger's admitted entry/sequence under the same new definition name so fact validation succeeds; require same-scope guard refusal and unchanged cursor.\n\nLater evidence: only after root grants executable work, compile the lending contexts and run the new owner plus affected old lending owners, with one meaningful same-scope guard control if required; run one gate at the eventual review head. File exact head, changed paths, nine witness names/file, source correspondence and durable logs. CUT-A currently owns executable work.\n\nCUT-R interaction is explicit. R1 at builder/cut-r-r1-20261114 will commit examples/lending/release-identifiers.json from canonical pack sources; no IDs file exists yet. R1 holds entry/other-definition/semantic/presentation IDs but no signature or release digest. Planner signs at R1 main only after those IDs match. R2 imports public packet/constants with unchanged canonical inputs. A roles/manifest change alters semantic identity even with unchanged shipped definition/pin, so P1 will neither regenerate that baseline nor silently change the pending packet. Release boundary 38c7c579 must govern metadata before code. No source edit, key/credential file read, network/Git-host write, test/compiler/build/generation/install/deploy/landing occurred in this preparation.","body":{"conditions":"Concrete P1 source plan and all nine witnesses before code. Metadata and authenticated Git boundary questions remain pending. No executable work while CUT-A holds the slot.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"planner"}}